committer hackerman-kl <alexandremalki89@gmail.com> 1788417945 +0200

The returning verification layer proves its own assertions can fail: the gasket and tsngen suites gain mutation arms, and each records what it still cannot reach

The two suites that came back with the verification layer assert a great
deal and proved none of it could fail. A harness whose assertions have
never been observed to fail is indistinguishable from one that asserts
nothing, and these two are the layer's judges: the gasket suite is the
one that pins the defect the MII gasket was repaired for, and tsngen is
the independent judge, driving the engine with frames a generator this
repository does not own builds.

Each suite now mutates the REAL RTL, one defect at a time, and requires
the SAME harness to fail. A positive control requires the unmutated build
to pass, without which the arm would be satisfied by a harness that fails
on everything. Mutants are built in a temporary directory and tsngen is
staged into one whole, so nothing is written into the tree and the
tracked microcode image is held constant while only the RTL varies.

The gasket arm injects four defects, all caught: a TX FIFO level
truncated below its full width, which is exactly the bug the gasket was
repaired for - a FIFO holding 64 words reads level 0 and wedges S_IDLE
forever; the egress and ingress SFD toggles frozen, which is where the
timestamp point is marked; and an end-of-frame never raised.

The tsngen arm injects three, all caught: the received sequenceId zeroed,
so a Follow_Up can no longer pair with its Sync; the Announce
grandmasterIdentity discarded, so BMCA compares a constant; and a
transmit end-of-frame one byte early. It skips exactly when the suite
skips, since run_tsngen.py exits 0 with a SKIP line where no tsn-gen
checkout exists and there is then nothing to prove.

"Caught" is read from the harness's own tally, in one place both arms
share. A non-zero exit alone is not a catch: a mutant that aborts, hangs
or dies by a signal has said nothing about the assertions, and each of
those outcomes is named as what it is rather than counted as success.

What the arms could NOT reach is recorded in each file rather than
hidden, because that map is half the value. Four real defects survived:
in the gasket suite, removing the start threshold entirely and a
read-side level off by one; in tsngen, a parser that accepts a foreign
domainNumber - the generator only ever builds domain-0 frames - and a
discarded received stepsRemoved. Those need new checks and new scenarios,
not new mutants.

`make` passes end to end: 768 ucpu, 268 parser, 664 engine, 81 gasket and
285 tsngen checks, the Arty bench tag test, both new arms at 5/5 and 4/4,
and the diagram and documentation gates.

